SQL> 
SQL> -- INTENT:
SQL> -- Purpose: Deploy the todo demo application -- one table, one package, its permissions and its
SQL> --   role -- so road-kit's own framework features can be exercised in road-kit.
SQL> -- Approach: Table, index and trigger, then the package, then the seed, then verification.
SQL> -- Reason: Three framework features are untestable without an application: the RESERVED
SQL> --   application permission (spec-patch-07 section 3.1's worked example),
SQL> --   grant_all_app_permissions, and the "an application extends the role model" pattern.
SQL> -- Expected objects: DEMO_TODOS, DEMO_TODOS_OWNER_STATUS, DEMO_TODOS_UPDATED_AT_TRG,
SQL> --   DEMO_TODO_API (+ _TEST), 7 permissions, 1 role.
SQL> -- Risk: Low, and confined -- every object is demo_/todo. prefixed.
SQL> -- Prior history checked: build-plan-08 phase 5.
SQL> -- END INTENT
SQL> 
SQL> -- NOT INVOKED BY deploy/create/00_full.sql, DELIBERATELY (spec-patch-08 section 3.1).
SQL> --
SQL> -- Two failure modes this placement avoids. In 00_full.sql, every adopter deploys todo tables and
SQL> -- then deletes them, and road-kit stops being clean to adopt -- which is the one thing it is for.
SQL> -- Kept fully separate and never run, the demo rots, and an unexercised demo is worse than none.
SQL> --
SQL> -- Resolution: this file is run unconditionally by whatever deploys road_kit_dev, and by nobody
SQL> -- else. Dev is the exercise environment; adopters get the framework alone.
SQL> --
SQL> -- 97_, after 96_assertions.sql, is also deliberate: this seeds a RESERVED permission, so the
SQL> -- assertions must already exist to validate that seed rather than be validated by it.
